A||N||13||bHooper||jumpy oil pressure gauge||||1||
Z||000000||bHooper||01-23-2001||12:14 PM||||my oil pressure gauge has been real jumpy, lately.  it is all over the place at different RPM's.  is this something serious?  or just a bad sending unit?  <P>i noticed on friday that it was pegging, so i changed the oil and filter, but that didn't seem to help very much.<P>thanks!<BR>hoop<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||1
Z||000001||Standard||01-23-2001||01:23 PM||||Just the sending unit going bad.  Mine does the same thing.  Although, it.. uhhh.. bounces accuratly, I guess you could say.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  It read low when my oil was old and dirty, but now it reads a bit higher with new 10w-40 in there... well, when my engine speed is steady so is the needle, but when I'm accelerating it gets pretty crazy.  Mine also usually stays pegged after I start my car, until it warms up a bit.  Confused me for a bit when it started working a few months ago, because it didn't when I got the car and I hadn't replaced it..||||reg||1
Z||000002||kinboyatuwo||01-23-2001||01:26 PM||||Same thing here and have had this for a while<BR>hope the problem is not big<P>the fourm has discussed the problem and solutions before though<P>------------------<BR>"Friends don't let friends drive four doors."||||reg||4
Z||000003||bHooper||01-23-2001||01:30 PM||||yeah, this thing is kinda wild all over the place.  it will peg under flat throttle, or read "accurate" under acceleration, or jump around at idle.  <P>crazy, i tell you!<P>one thing i do wish, is that i had <B>never</B> installed those white gauge plates on the car.  ever since i put those on, they are now off, i have never had a acurate needle yet!  it scares the hell outa me!<P>is there any good way to check and "calibrate" the gauges, without being a engineer?<P>thanks!<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000004||Standard||01-23-2001||01:46 PM||||Get a good ole' mechanical oil pressure gauge  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><P>I must say tho, that I did like it better when my gauge just didn't work.. before I changed my oil the pressure was pretty low at idle, and sometimes it would bounce into the red zone and light up the idiot light.  Always made my heart jump...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>As for calibrating.. measure whatever value it is for the gauge that you're calibrating, then pull the needle off and put it back in the right position... like for the voltmeter, measure the voltage at the battery with the car at idle (should be around 14.7) and stick the needle on at that position.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  For the coolant temp you'll probably need an ECM scanner.||||reg||1
Z||000005||bHooper||01-23-2001||01:50 PM||||well, at least the red light has <B>never</B> come on.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Bob Englert||01-23-2001||06:46 PM||||I wish I could say that about the red light Hoop!<P>On both GT's the red light pops on moentarily when idling and fully warmed up.  I have changed the sending unit in the maroon GT which was bouncing around but I haven't gotten the plenum back on yet from the EGR tube replacement to see if it is steady again.  Hopefully I will have it back together Sunday.<P>I also plan to change the oil filter bypass check valve on both cars to see if that helps the low oil pressure at idle.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000007||bHooper||01-23-2001||09:24 PM||||strange cars, indeed!  on the way home from work (the fun way), the gauge was relatively stable!  reading about 40-50 at idle and 60-70 at full throttle!<P>go figure!<P>when i have the money, and time, i am going to replace everyone of these old, worn out, horible GM gauges with new high quality analoge units!<P>with the technical help of the forum, that is  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>hoop<P><BR>p.s.<BR>bob, you gotta get that maroon car together.  have you tried changing the sending unit on the blue car, yet?  with the power that car has, i can't imagine it having anything seriously wrong with it.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||DJRice||01-23-2001||09:41 PM||||My brothers 86 was the same way.  We just replaced the sending unit last weekend.  It was jumping around like the house of pain and the funny thing is that the car would occasionally stall.  I figured it was because the bad sending unit was activating the fuel shut off relay because it was sensing no oil pressure.  Actually, the oil pump was going bad too.  <P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>"You mean like the back seat of a Volkswagen?"||||reg||1
Z||000009||2birds||01-24-2001||08:58 PM||||I don't know if you guys saw the post on this last week, but I put my experience with a bad sending unit in that one.<BR>The sending unit can fail high, which bypasses the fuel pump relay and causes your fuel pump to run continuously (or until the battery runs dead, as happened to me).  <BR>If your OP meter is jumping all over, it's about had it.  Replace your sending unit before this happens to you.<P>I've changed mine twice in 13 years, and they're cheap enough.||||reg||1
Z||000010||bHooper||01-24-2001||09:28 PM||||again, the oil pressure gauge seemed "normal" today.<P>i will definately replace it.<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||1
Z||000011||Smokin87||01-24-2001||09:49 PM||||mine does the same thing...just change the sending unit, for some reason alot of fieros have that problem.  go figure.  <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero_20.jpg"> <BR>Justin Coe||||reg||1
Z||000012||Standard||01-25-2001||03:04 PM||||The problem with the sending unit is the vent hole in the top of it.  It's also right under the grill, so water finds it's way inside there pretty easily and starts corroding things.  Not the best design.. I've heard it's a good idea to seal that hole with some RTV if you want one to last any amount of time...<P>When my sending unit didn't work, it was pegged, but I didn't have any problems with the fuel pump running.||||reg||
Z||000013||GarethWright||01-25-2001||03:57 PM||||My Oil pressure meter bounces around when I am stopped in Drive, If I put it in Neutral or Park the meter stops bouncing, also It reads fairly bounce-less-ly whenever I am driving, could a bad sender unit cause my problems?||||reg||1
